WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.141
We all know the story of Mowgli 

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.776
from Rudyard Kipling's 

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.177
"The Jungle Book", 

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.278
about the boy 

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.681
who was brought up by wolves.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:17.717
Or Edgar Rice Burrough's Tarzan, 

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.987
who was raised by chimpanzees.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.856
And there's the story 

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.258
of Romulus and Remus, 

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.060
the founders of Rome, 

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.662
suckled by a wolf in a cave.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.264
Eww.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:34.467
But can humans really 

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.003
be raised by animals?

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.539
And if so, how would 

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.709
they adapt to society?

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:51.451
Feral children are children who

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.919
 don't have interactions

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.854
with other humans. 

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.924
There are about 4,000 accounts 

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.526
of feral children that

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.428
 are considered reliable. 

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.696
Sadly, most of these cases 

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.765
are due to neglect. 

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.802
Here are three incredible stories 

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:12.839
of humans raised by animals.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.545
This is Marina Chapman. 

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:21.614
In 2012, she published a book 

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.184
about being raised by monkeys 

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.719
in the jungles of Columbia.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.756
In 1950, when she was a young child, 

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.826
Chapman was abandoned in a forest. 

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.628
She almost died until a family 

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.363
of capuchin monkeys 

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.266
led her to fruit and nuts.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.601
The monkeys took her in 

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.602
and protected her. 

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.872
But she still had to fend for herself, 

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.341
taking food when she could.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.543
When she was about nine years old, 

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.378
she was discovered by people

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.647
 who, sadly, sold her 

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.117
into domestic slavery.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.052
She ran away and lived on the streets, 

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.553
where she learned to speak 

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.990
and used her jungle skills to survive.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.159
Eventually, she was able to

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.961
conform to modern society 

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:11.998
and even married and had children.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.472
This is Marcos Pantoja. 

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.408
After losing his mother at an early age, 

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.978
Marcos suffered an abusive upbringing

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.846
 from his stepmother. 

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.315
At the age of six, his father

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.451
 sold him to a goat farmer 

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:32.719
in a remote area 

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.821
of the Sierra Morena mountain range 

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.122
in Spain. 

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:38.725
When the farmer died two years later, 

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.428
Marcos was left to fend for himself.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.365
While exploring the mountains for food, 

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.833
Marcos came across 

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.968
a wolf cub in a cave. 

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.971
After playing with the cub, he fell asleep 

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.674
and woke later to find the mother

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.911
growling and baring her teeth at him.

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.046
Marcos backed away.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.915
After feeding her cubs, 

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.816
the mother offered some of 

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.252
the leftover meat to the boy. 

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.221
From then on, 

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.623
Marcos lived as a member 

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:14.093
of the wolfpack for 12 years.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.896
He was found by Spanish Civil Guards, 

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:19.032
who bound and gagged him 

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.833
to keep him from howling. 

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.303
They took him home to his father. 

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:25.538
Wanting nothing to do with Marcos, 

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.607
his father took him to a hospital 

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.375
run by nuns. 

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.377
There he was taught to speak,

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.779
 walk upright, 

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.080
dress properly,

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.716
and eat with cutlery. 

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.051
The feral upbringing

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.753
 left Marcos traumatized. 

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.088
He fought with the nuns 

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.389
when they tried to get him 

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.724
to sleep in a bed. 

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.026
And he feared he was being attacked 

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:48.928
during his first haircut.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.663
After serving in the military 

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.632
and working with a pastor 

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.900
for many years, 

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.935
Marcos struggled to adapt

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.104
 to modern society.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.405
 Feeling isolated, 

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.474
he returned to the mountains 

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.610
to live with the animals. 

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.279
Unfortunately, his wolf family 

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.280
rejected him

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.816
because of his human scent.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:17.790
This is Oxana Malaya. 

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:21.527
In 1991, at the age of three, 

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.696
she was left outside 

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.065
by her alcoholic parents. 

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.401
She crawled into a dog kennel

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:30.403
 for shelter and warmth.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:33.039
Oxana spent the next five years 

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.842
with the dogs, where she ate scraps 

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.210
left by the animals.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.979
A neighbor noticed her at eight years old

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.614
living in the kennel.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.816
 She ran on all fours, 

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.551
barked like a dog, 

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.120
panted with her tongue out 

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.988
and would bare her teeth. 

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.757
She couldn't talk.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.725
"Can't talk."

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.228
Once a child passes the age of five

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.562
 without learning to talk,

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.865
 it is almost impossible for them 

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.366
to learn to speak normally.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:01.768
"Can you say hello?"

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:04.070
Oxana, however, did speak 

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.371
before she was abandoned 

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.473
and was able to relearn 

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.941
how to communicate.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.611
It took six months to suppress 

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.946
her dog-like behavior.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.416
Now an adult, she is able to speak 

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:19.018
and eats with her hands instead of 

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.621
lapping up her food with her tongue.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:24.123
But she still has moments 

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.658
when she goes back 

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.527
to her feral upbringing, 

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:29.629
like crawling on all fours 

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:31.664
when she feels lonely.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.633
It is estimated that she has 

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:37.470
the mental capacity of a six-year-old.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.705
Now that we've seen 

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:41.441
that feral children are real, 

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:43.943
we'll discover if humans 

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.746
can have superpowers 

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.514
on another episode of

